Where's the elevation preview tracking?? The latest update that removed this feature is a terrible idea (where you could preview elevation change along a route by sliding your finger across the elevation graph). This was incredibly helpful in terms of route-planning, and the "preview trail" feature just isn't robust enough to provide the same level of detail. Agree with others, paying for pro seem like a waste now. Please reinstate as this was a highly beneficial feature. REPLY-thanks 4 update!-[split]-Hi update! We are sorry to hear that. Try clearing the app's data and cache (not photos), then restart your phone to the most topics to the app. We would love to get in touch with us.
I have been using the app for several years and subscribed last year to download maps. Very happy until latest update. The blue dot elevation tracker that showed where you are on the trail and profile was removed. This was a great useful feature and should be replaced ASAP. In a related issue... the 3d preview is not at all accurate in respect to elevation gain. It has no connection to the actual trail terrain and simply tics up at a constant average rate to match the distance.-[split]-Hi distance. We are sorry to hear that. Try clearing the app's data and cache (not photos), then restart your phone to the latest version. If you have any further assistance, please reach out to us at <EMAIL> with any further distance.
Latest update removed ability to see a blue dot on the map corresponding to where you trace your finger along the elevation chart. This function is probably the most valuable thing this app does. Without it, trip planning and simple on-trail progress tracking without recording can no longer be done from my phone. I submitted an email and alltrails responded that they do not know when this will be fixed. What were you guys thinking?? Why am I paying for this app? Please fix this now!-[split]-Hi now! We are sorry to hear that. Try clearing the app's data and cache (not photos), then restart your phone to the latest version. If you have any further assistance, please reach out to us at <EMAIL> with any further now!
