Annoying "playback can't be played on this device" error a lot of the time and long pauses when starting a track (if I don't get above error). Sound quality is excellent and full Hi res flac files is great. Pitty about clunky app. Spotify app would be the easiest to use (not audiophile quality though), then tidal and this app last (fail for me). You can use this through third party software like USB audio pro. But rather use app on the go. Thinking about unsubscribing. I'm using a S21 ultra.-[split]-Dear ultra. Thank you for your feedback. We are excited to have enthusiastic people like you in our family ! Musically yours, The Qobuz Team
The sound quality is awesome, and there aren't that many gaps in their library. I can think of a few I'd like to add, but I'm quite happy. Where Qobuz loses a point is the somewhat confusing UI, a very weird listing of an artist's releases where many seem to be covers by others, and a search function that is surprisingly rigid. There should be a way to search properly without having to specify if you are looking for an artist, a release, or something else.-[split]-Dear else. Thank you for your kind review ! We are excited to have enthusiastic people like you in our family ! Musically yours, The Qobuz Team
If you have an account that's not premium, this prevents you from logging in (also the website covers the login button with a banner ad, so you have to log in by passing through the terms & conditions page). The app also doesn't recognize when you DO sign up for a paid account. The shuffle feature and the queue both turn the other off. It forgets genre preferences regularly. This is scratching the surface of how bad the app is. But there's a good selection of music, that plays at good quality.-[split]-Dear also Thank you for your kind review ! We are excited to have enthusiastic people like you in our family ! Musically yours, The Qobuz Team
I want to use this as it seems qobuz pays artists the most out of the streaming services (why don't they advertise this as I can't be the only one interested in it!) But there's one major problem. The releases for artists aren't ordered at all, if you don't know the artist discography there is no way of telling what is an album or a single or even when they were released. Perhaps I have missed the option to sort them but if I have it isn't obvious. Fix this and I would happily switch provider-[split]-Dear provider Thank you for your feedback. We are excited to have enthusiastic people like you in our family ! Musically yours, The Qobuz Team
